= January 2024 — The audience has found another address

Tomasz Sakiewicz, editor-in-chief of TV Republika, is receiving presenters,
viewers and donations displaced by the public-media fight. Former TVP anchor
Danuta Holecka gives the migration a familiar face. Advertisers withdrawing
from the channel discover that every cancelled placement can also be sold as
proof of a boycott.

The route here matters. The government chose **[+ public_media_transition +]**
while Lewica built **[+ media_relationship +]**.
[? if public_media_transition = "Rapid corporate transition": The rapid
takeover gave displaced presenters a shared grievance and a destination.?]
[? if public_media_transition = "Statutory reform behind the veto wall":
Partisan broadcasting lasted longer, but the legal case for persecution is
weaker.?]
[? if public_media_transition = "Interim pluralist board": The truce preserved
some conservative access; Republika grows as a rival, not a refugee newsroom.?]

- @republika_neutral
- @republika_pressure
- @republika_build

@republika_neutral
title: Defend advertiser choice and reject government pressure
subtitle: Let companies leave or return on their own; Republika may grow, but it cannot plausibly make Lewica the censor.
on-arrival: media_relationship = "Pluralist rules and independent distribution"; government_procedural_restraint += 3; public_trust += 2; republika_capacity += 2; media_capacity += 1; news_headline = "The Left refuses to turn a boycott into state censorship"

We say publicly that a private company may refuse Sakiewicz's audience and may
also change its mind without a call from a ministry. The remaining advertisers
and journalists know the rule applies to friendly outlets too.

Republika converts some departures into subscriptions, but the state-
persecution campaign lacks a state instruction. We defend a hostile channel's
freedom without financing its grievance for it.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the advertiser rule to the events desk

@republika_pressure
title: Ask state companies to review every placement
subtitle: Withdraw public advertising from a hostile channel; give Sakiewicz evidence that the new state is organising the boycott.
on-arrival: {!
Q.media_relationship = "Pressure on hostile private media";
Q.republika_capacity += 7;
Q.government_procedural_restraint -= 5;
Q.pis_poll_momentum += 0.3;
Q.far_right_agenda += 2;
Q.public_trust -= 2;
if (Q.government_party == "ko") {
    Q.ko_poll_momentum -= 0.45;
    if (Q.left_in_government) Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.2;
    if (Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet) Q.psl_poll_momentum -= 0.1;
    if (Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet) Q.p2050_poll_momentum -= 0.1;
}
Q.news_headline =
    "Commercial pressure gives Republika a state-persecution story";
!}

State companies receive the message and their campaigns disappear from
Republika's schedule. The loss hurts ordinary revenue before the first new
subscription arrives.

Sakiewicz publishes the calls and turns procurement into persecution. Viewers
who might have drifted away now pay to keep the channel alive; PiS gains a
private broadcaster with a founding injury supplied by the government.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the state-advertising decision on the events desk

@republika_build
title: Use the opening to finance an independent Left newsroom
subtitle: Cost: 3 resources. Hire reporters and federate local outlets rather than trying to silence somebody else's audience.
choose-if: resources >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot capitalize a newsroom.
on-arrival: resources -= 3; media_relationship = "Owned newsroom and federated local distribution"; media_capacity += 9; local_network += 2; barons_dissent += 2; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The Left finally invests in a media institution of its own"

The party hires a small reporting desk and gives local union and municipal
outlets a common distribution system. It cannot match Republika's audience
this month, but the next hostile invitation is no longer the only way our
argument reaches a screen.

Old hands resent an institution they do not personally control. Reporters gain
a budget, subscribers gain an address and Lewica assumes the obligations of a
publisher instead of merely demanding better bookings.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the new newsroom on the events desk

@konkrety_fifty_days_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — the fifty-day count, the Palace arrests eating the cycle and KO's unnamed "coalition partners" briefing are staged as one manoeuvre, and each Lewica route changes whether the blame stays unaddressed, gets a name, or gets a spreadsheet.
title: Fifty days, three konkrety
subtitle: The first audits land while KO briefs that delivery is slow because of unnamed coalition partners
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-press-gallery.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 26
order: 6
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 1 and government_party = "ko" and caretaker_government = 0 and konkrety_stage = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_stage = 2;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_salience += 4;
Q.news_headline =
    "Fifty-day audits find three konkrety delivered and no minister who owns the rest";
!}

= January 2024 — Three out of a hundred

The fact-checking outfits publish at the halfway mark and the number is three.
Three of the hundred konkrety are complete: the anti-violence policy work
begun, the European money released, and a Ministry of Industry seated in
Silesia. Forty-odd others are described as *in progress*, which is a category
the government invented for this occasion and the auditors accepted under
protest.

The number should be the week's story. It is not, because on 9 January police
enter the Presidential Palace and remove **Mariusz Kamiński** and **Maciej
Wąsik** — the former interior minister and his deputy, convicted, stripped of
their mandates, and sheltered by the President until the moment they were not.
Everything else in politics stops for a fortnight. The Chancellery's press
operation does nothing to restart it.

What the Chancellery does do is brief. Not on the record and not with names:
the line given to political correspondents is that the hundred konkrety are
moving slowly because a coalition of four parties cannot move faster, and that
some partners are more of an obstacle than others. **Mariusz Witczak** of KO
says the printable version out loud — *if we had a homogeneous government, if
KO had won 231 seats, we would have the opportunity to be accountable for these
hundred promises*.

No partner is named. That is the whole design: three parties spend the weekend
denying something nobody accused them of, and the party that wrote the list
spends it being sympathised with.

[? if konkrety_line = "Publicly refused the list": Our December refusal is
quoted in every one of those briefings, without the sentence that followed it,
and it reads exactly as intended.?]
[? if konkrety_line = "Co-signed the hundred konkrety": We adopted this list in
December as the government's own. The briefings do not mention that either, and
we are being counted among the obstacles to a programme we signed.?]
[? if konkrety_receipts = 1: We have the annex. Every item we took, with a
ministry and a month beside it, filed before any of this started.?]
[? if kpo_shortcut_debt > 0: One of the three delivered konkrety is the
European money, which arrived on terms we shortened in 2023 and will be asked
about again.?]

**Anna Maria Żukowska** wants to answer publicly and is asking the leadership
for permission rather than forgiveness.

- @fifty_names
- @fifty_scoreboard
- @fifty_billing
- @fifty_ledger
- @fifty_shield

@fifty_names
title: Demand that KO name the partners it means
subtitle: Forces an anonymous briefing into the open where it can be contradicted; the coalition spends a week on itself instead of on PiS.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_answer = "Demanded names";
Q.konkrety_ownership = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.konkrety_ownership) || 0) - 10
);
Q.media_capacity += 4;
Q.parliament_visibility += 3;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.ko_relation -= 6;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 5;
Q.psl_relation += 3;
Q.p2050_relation += 2;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left asks the Prime Minister to name the coalition partners he means";
!}

Żukowska puts the question in public and does not decorate it: which partners,
which konkrety, which meetings. Name them.

The Chancellery cannot answer. Naming PSL in January costs the government its
agriculture policy in February; naming us costs it the votes it needs for the
budget. So the briefing stops, the correspondents note that it stopped, and
the phrase *unnamed coalition partners* acquires a shelf life it would not
otherwise have had.

Paszyk telephones to say thank you, which is the first warm minute PSL and
Lewica have shared since the formation. Tusk does not telephone. The cost is
that a coalition eight weeks old has now had its first public argument about
whose fault something is, and everyone watching learned the format.

- @poland_event_queue: Ask him to name them

@fifty_scoreboard
title: Propose a delivery committee that publishes a named scoreboard each month
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Replaces briefing wars with arithmetic; the March audit then argues with a published document rather than with us.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A monthly cross-ministry audit needs staff the party does not have free.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.konkrety_answer = "Built the delivery scoreboard";
Q.konkrety_scoreboard = 1;
Q.government_delivery += 3;
Q.institutional_trust += 4;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.negotiation_capital += 1;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.government_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 2
);
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "A coalition delivery committee will publish a named scoreboard every month";
!}

We answer the briefing with a procedure. A standing coalition committee, one
delegate per party, meeting monthly, publishing a single table: konkret,
responsible ministry, legal instrument, status, blocking party where there is
one.

KO agrees, because refusing a transparency proposal in the eighth week of a
government elected on transparency is not survivable. It agrees having
understood the cost about a day too late: an anonymous briefing works only
against an opponent who cannot produce a document, and from February there will
be a document every month with somebody's name in the blocking column.

The table is dull, it will never trend, and it converts the whole hundred-days
question from a fight about tone into a fight about rows.

- @poland_event_queue: Convene the committee

@fifty_billing
title: Insist on joint billing: we signed it, so we announce it
subtitle: Requires having co-signed the list. Takes a share of the podium for the delivered konkrety; the undelivered ones then belong to us just as visibly.
choose-if: konkrety_ownership >= 60
unavailable-subtitle: We never adopted the list as ours, so there is no signature entitling us to stand behind the Prime Minister while he reads it out.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_answer = "Took joint billing";
Q.konkrety_ownership += 10;
Q.konkrety_left_credit += 1;
Q.ko_relation += 5;
Q.government_delivery += 2;
Q.media_capacity += 3;
Q.parliament_visibility += 4;
Q.coalition_blur += 4;
Q.movement_autonomy = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.movement_autonomy) || 47) - 3);
Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left demands equal billing on every konkret the government delivers";
!}

If the list is the government's programme — and in December we said it was —
then the government's programme is announced by the government, not by one
party's press office. Our ministers appear beside KO's at every delivery
announcement from now on, and the party logo goes on the slides.

It works. The industry ministry in Katowice is announced with three parties on
the platform, and for the first time since the formation a piece of delivery
reads as a coalition act rather than as Tusk keeping a promise.

We have also just stood, on camera, in front of a scoreboard reading three out
of a hundred. There is no version of joint billing that applies only to the
completed rows.

- @poland_event_queue: Take the podium

@fifty_ledger
title: Publish the December annex before the deflection sets
subtitle: Requires the written annex. Puts our owned items and their real status into the public record while the briefing is still anonymous.
choose-if: konkrety_receipts = 1
unavailable-subtitle: We wrote nothing down in December, so there is no ledger to publish and nothing to contradict the briefing with.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_answer = "Published the annex";
Q.konkrety_left_credit += 2;
Q.media_capacity += 3;
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.institutional_trust += 3;
Q.parliament_visibility += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 3;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 3;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.15;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica publishes what it signed for in December, item by item";
!}

We put the annex on the website with the status of each line beside it, and we
do it while the accusation is still unnamed, which is the only week in which
doing so looks like transparency rather than defence.

The effect is narrow and real. Three or four correspondents now have a document
that says which konkrety were ever ours, and they start asking the Chancellery
for the equivalent list for the other ninety. There is no equivalent list. The
briefings continue, but the sentence *the government has not published which
minister owns which promise* enters the coverage and does not leave it.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the ledger

@fifty_shield
title: Absorb it and defend the government's record in public
subtitle: The coalition's calmest month; the deflection goes unchallenged and hardens into the version everyone repeats in March.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_answer = "Shielded the government";
Q.konkrety_ownership += 15;
Q.ko_relation += 8;
Q.government_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 5
);
Q.government_delivery += 1;
Q.coalition_blur += 5;
Q.movement_autonomy = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.movement_autonomy) || 47) - 5);
Q.progressive_credibility = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) - 3
);
Q.progressives_dissent += 4;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left defends the government's delivery record and asks for patience";
!}

Our spokespeople go out and say that eight weeks is eight weeks, that the
ministries were found in a worse state than anybody admitted in the campaign,
and that a coalition of four parties negotiating in public would deliver
nothing at all. All of which is true.

Tusk is grateful and says so privately. The correspondents write that even the
Left is defending the pace, which is a better sentence for the Chancellery than
anything its own briefers produced.

The version of events in which the coalition partners are the problem is now
eleven weeks old, unchallenged, and repeated by us. In March it will not be
possible to argue with it, because the archive will show that we did not.

- @poland_event_queue: Defend the record

# Research:
# https://www.bankier.pl/wiadomosc/Roman-Giertych-na-czele-zespolu-ktory-bedzie-rozliczal-PiS-8680729.html
# https://www.rp.pl/polityka/art38939181-anna-maria-zukowska-wbrew-deklaracjom-roman-giertych-sie-tak-bardzo-nie-zmienil
@giertych_reckoning_team_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Giertych's LPR ministry, his years as Tusk's lawyer and his new coordinating body are all established before Lewica speaks, and Żukowska's objection is quoted rather than summarised, so the choice is about what the Left says on the record, not whether it dislikes him.
title: KO gives the reckoning a chairman
subtitle: The team that will settle eight years of PiS is chaired by the deputy prime minister who put the far right in a Polish cabinet
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-new-deputies-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 27
order: 4
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 1 and government_party != "pis" and reckoning_team_2024_done = 0 and (ko_leader = "Donald Tusk" or ko_leader = "Radosław Sikorski")
on-arrival: {!
Q.reckoning_team_2024_done = 1;
Q.reckoning_team_active = 1;
Q.reckoning_stage = 1;
Q.reckoning_delivery = 0;
Q.reckoning_noise = 8;
// The August 2023 list decision already set his weight inside KO. The
// chairmanship adds to whatever the player left him with; it does not reset it.
Q.giertych_standing = Math.min(
    100, (Number(Q.giertych_standing) || 38) + 8
);
// KO's own centre of gravity moves when its accountability programme is
// handed to a national-conservative. This is a real wing shift, not a label:
// the drift model in poland_party_ai reads the wing shares, so a change made
// only to ko_cultural_position would be erased within two months.
Q.ko_social_liberal_share = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.ko_social_liberal_share) || 42) - 3
);
Q.ko_classical_liberal_share = Math.min(
    100, (Number(Q.ko_classical_liberal_share) || 58) + 3
);
Q.ko_right_score = (Number(Q.ko_right_score) || 50) + 4;
Q.ko_cultural_position = (Number(Q.ko_cultural_position) || 43) + 2;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 8;
Q.news_headline =
    "KO's club puts Roman Giertych in charge of settling accounts with PiS";
!}

= January 2024 — The man who will do the settling

The Civic Coalition club establishes a **Zespół do spraw rozliczeń** — a
coordinating team for the eight years of PiS government. It is not a
prosecuting body and not a Sejm inquiry: it collects material, files
notifications with prosecutors, and pushes ministries to move faster on
administrative and criminal proceedings. Its chairman is **Roman Giertych**,
Civic Coalition deputy for Kielce.

Everyone in this room knows the whole of that name. In 2006 Giertych led the
**League of Polish Families**, which he had built out of the **All-Polish
Youth**, and became deputy prime minister and minister of education in Jarosław
Kaczyński's cabinet. He purged reading lists, ran a national campaign against
what he called homosexual propaganda in schools, and proposed uniformed
discipline for every classroom. It was the first time since 1989 that the far
right sat in a Polish government, and our people were the ones standing outside
the ministry.

Since then he has been **[+ ko_leader +]**'s lawyer, and PiS made him a
defendant:
Ziobro's prosecutors staged his detention in 2020, seized his files in front of
cameras, and he collapsed during it. He came back into public life as the most
determined enemy the men who did it have, and in October he came back into the
Sejm on KO's list. **[+ ko_leader +]** trusts him completely, and says so — and
that trust is the entire mechanism here. Nobody else in the Civic Coalition
would have given him this body, and everybody in it knows that.

**Anna Maria Żukowska**, chair of our own parliamentary club, has already given
the Left's answer in public, and she gave it before the election: that despite
his declarations *he has not changed that much*, and that if he were as
well-liked as everyone claims, somebody would have put him on the senate pact —
and nobody did, because nobody wanted to own his votes on partnerships and
abortion. That position has a second half she repeats whenever she is asked:
she will not sit in a government with him.

[? if giertych_line = "Pact refusal stated publicly": In August we said in
public why the Senate pact carried no joint candidate in his case. Every
journalist in the building has that quote and knows we are about to be asked
whether it still applies to a coordinating body.?]
[? if giertych_line = "Democratic-camp endorsement": In August we called him
part of the democratic camp on the record. That sentence is now the first
result anybody finds, and KO's briefers have already sent it round.?]
[? if giertych_line = "Silence during the campaign": In August we declined to
discuss KO's list at all. The advantage of having said nothing is that nothing
has to be withdrawn; the disadvantage arrives now, because this is the second
time and the offices are real.?]

None of that stops the team existing. It exists, it has a chairman, and it will
be the face of the one thing our voters most want this government to do.

- @giertych_terms
- @giertych_red_line
- @giertych_join
- @giertych_silence

@giertych_terms
title: Demand written terms: the team may coordinate, never instruct a prosecutor
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Treat him as a procedural risk rather than a biography; the safeguard survives him and slows him down.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The parliamentary legal team has no capacity to draft and defend the protocol.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; giertych_line = "Written limits on the reckoning team"; reckoning_delivery += 8; reckoning_noise -= 4; giertych_standing -= 4; government_procedural_restraint += 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 3; public_trust += 2; ko_relation -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica forces written limits on the coalition's reckoning team"

Our lawyers write the rule and make KO sign it: the team may gather material,
publish findings and file notifications like any citizen, and it may not
transmit an expectation to a named prosecutor about a named case. Every
contact with the prosecution service is logged.

Giertych accepts, because refusing would have been the story. The protocol is
dull, it will be quoted at us the next time we hold Justice, and it is the only
thing here that will still be doing work in four years.

- @poland_event_queue: File the protocol

@giertych_red_line
title: Put Żukowska's condition on the record: never in a cabinet with him
subtitle: Say the thing the Left's voters want said and hand Tusk a public quarrel with his most trusted man.
on-arrival: giertych_line = "Public veto on Giertych in government"; giertych_standing -= 9; progressive_credibility += 6; ko_relation -= 7; ko_coalition_dissent += 5; razem_cooperation += 5; progressives_dissent -= 5; spring_dissent -= 3; public_trust += 1; left_poll_momentum += 0.2; news_headline = "Lewica declares that Giertych will never sit in a cabinet it belongs to"

Żukowska says it from the club's own rostrum, with dates: the reading lists,
the ministry circulars, the campaign against teachers. Coordinating a reckoning
is one thing. A ministry is another, and there is no version of this coalition
in which the Left votes for him.

KO's press office calls it an unnecessary quarrel about a job nobody has
offered. Tusk does not answer publicly, which in his case is an answer. We have
spent coalition warmth to buy a sentence our own voters will be able to check
later — and we have made the appointment, if it is ever attempted, into a
question about us.

- @poland_event_queue: Say it from the rostrum

@giertych_join
title: Take a Left seat on the team and work the files
subtitle: Access to the material and a share of the credit, bought by standing next to him in every photograph.
on-arrival: giertych_line = "Left seat on the reckoning team"; reckoning_delivery += 5; reckoning_noise += 3; giertych_standing += 6; ko_relation += 6; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 4; judicial_repair_mandate += 2; progressives_dissent += 7; razem_dissent += 8; razem_cooperation -= 6; progressive_credibility -= 5; news_headline = "Lewica joins the coalition's reckoning team"

Our deputy takes the seat, and it is worth something immediately: the Justice
Fund files, the media procurement, the Pegasus billing. We see the material at
the same time as KO instead of reading about it.

The photograph is the price. Razem publishes a statement the same evening about
the party of the anti-fascist left sitting in a body chaired by the founder of
the All-Polish Youth, and our own progressive deputies do not defend us in the
group chat. Both things are now true at once, permanently.

- @poland_event_queue: Take the seat

@giertych_silence
title: Treat the chairmanship as KO's internal business
subtitle: Spend nothing, promise nothing, and let the archive record that the Left had no comment on this appointment.
on-arrival: giertych_line = "No comment"; giertych_standing += 4; ko_relation += 2; reckoning_noise += 2; progressives_dissent += 4; progressive_credibility -= 3; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The Left declines to comment on KO's choice of chairman"

Another club may choose its own chairmen. We say so, briefly, and move the
briefing on to housing.

It costs nothing today. It also means that when somebody proposes him for an
office that requires our votes, the first thing every journalist will find is
the week we decided this was not our business.

- @poland_event_queue: Move the briefing on
